      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/McSherrystown%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The first recorded deed for a lot dates back to June 27, 1765.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/McSherrystown%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Although intended as outlots for Hanover, the settlement quickly grew into a full‑fledged town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/McSherrystown%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "McSherrystown is the fourth oldest town in Adams County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/McSherrystown%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "McSherrystown once housed Boyds Bears, a teddy‑bear manufacturer, and the oldest family‑run cigar shop in the U.S.",
